# =============================================================================
# ↦ — Matrix to tensor conversio.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Register-class to shaped conversion — a `matrix` converts into a shaped `tensor` when the target type witnesses a literal Figura.
#   • Same flat body — the matrix cells lower in row-major order into the tensor's flat storage.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Mismatching the matrix shape and the target tensor Figura — the element counts must agree.
#
# See also: ↦, matrix, tensor, Figura
# =============================================================================


# conversio — matrix to tensor
#
# WHY: the register-class matrix and the shaped tensor share their flat cell
# order, so the conversion carries the four elements row-major into the target
# Figura. `flatten` reads the tensor back flat.

main {
    let matrix<f32, [2, 2]> m ← [[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]] ↦ matrix<f32, [2, 2]>
    let tf32[2, 2] t ← m ↦ tf32[2, 2]
    print t.flatten()
}
